From: Satoshi Nakamoto <hello@chadwallet.xyz>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:23:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(browse): keep headed windows on BROWSER_DISPLAY and
 open tabs without taking focus

launchHeaded opens the window on the display BROWSER_DISPLAY names (from the
environment, else ~/.config/web/.env; any part of the name, any case; empty
means the main display) through --window-position, and moves windows that
open elsewhere back onto it whenever a page opens (displayOrigin.swift and
moveWindows.swift in browse/scripts/, macOS only, best-effort).

Headed newTab opens its page with CDP Target.createTarget({ background: true })
instead of context.newPage(), which could activate the browser window and take
macOS focus from the user's app.
